            <header class="lesson-header"><span class="lesson-number">Lesson 3</span><h1>Domain-Driven Design Basics</h1><div class="lesson-meta"><span class="lesson-duration"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/></svg>30 min</span><span class="lesson-level advanced">Advanced</span></div></header>
            <div class="lesson-body">
                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Bounded Contexts</h2>
                    <p>A bounded context defines the boundary within which a domain model applies. Different contexts can have different models for the same concept.</p>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">// In Sales Context
public class Customer
{
    public Guid Id { get; }
    public string Name { get; }
    public CreditLimit CreditLimit { get; }
    public List&lt;Order&gt; Orders { get; }
}

// In Shipping Context - different view of Customer
public class Customer  
{
    public Guid Id { get; }
    public ShippingAddress Address { get; }
    public DeliveryPreferences Preferences { get; }
}</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Aggregates</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">// Aggregate Root - the only entry point
public class Order
{
    public Guid Id { get; private set; }
    private readonly List&lt;OrderItem&gt; _items = new();
    public IReadOnlyList&lt;OrderItem&gt; Items =&gt; _items.AsReadOnly();
    
    public void AddItem(Product product, int quantity)
    {
        // Business logic and validation here
        var item = new OrderItem(product.Id, product.Price, quantity);
        _items.Add(item);
    }
}

// Part of the aggregate - accessed through Order
public class OrderItem
{
    public Guid ProductId { get; }
    public Money Price { get; }
    public int Quantity { get; }
}</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Domain Events</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">public record OrderPlaced(Guid OrderId, Guid CustomerId, decimal Total);

public class Order
{
    private readonly List&lt;IDomainEvent&gt; _events = new();
    
    public void Place()
    {
        Status = OrderStatus.Placed;
        _events.Add(new OrderPlaced(Id, CustomerId, Total));
    }
    
    public IEnumerable&lt;IDomainEvent&gt; GetDomainEvents() =&gt; _events;
}</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Context Mapping</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-text">Relationship Types:
- Shared Kernel: Both teams share a model
- Customer/Supplier: Downstream depends on upstream
- Conformist: Downstream conforms to upstream
- Anti-Corruption Layer: Translate between models
- Published Language: Shared communication format</code></pre>
                </section>

